    "updated_at": "2017-06-15T18:32:33Z",
    "body": "That's an interesting point.  As far as I can tell, Gecko gives any non-floated non-abs/fixedpos legend that's a child of a fieldset a block-inside box.  Depending on whether the original display was block-level or inline-level it basically acts like a block or inline-block.  This is not restricted to just the \"rendered legend\".  So I guess Gecko actually has two concepts: an \"in-flow legend in a fieldset\", which gets special box handling, and \"rendered legend\", which is the first \"in-flow legend in a fieldset\" for a given fiedset.\r\n\r\nWhat do other UAs do?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
