    "created_at": "2017-06-19T09:12:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-19T09:12:38Z",
    "body": "I would be OK with having a concept of \"potential rendered legend\", which is any legend that is a child of a fieldset (DOM child, possibly flat tree child if there's a use case for that).\r\n\r\nA potential rendered legend would always be a BFC and shrink-wrap, maybe even force display:block (if not display:none or display:contents).\r\n\r\nPer https://drafts.csswg.org/css-display/#unbox-html , CSS WG consensus is that display:contents should work on fieldset and legend. I think it would be nice to have it work, and there's at least a recent [tweet](https://twitter.com/ThatEmil/status/875628910372806659) wishing for the same. So how about display:contents on fieldset means it can't have any potential rendered legend, and a legend with `display:contents` has no magic.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/309383430/reactions",
